<title>USA: U.S. to back fewer supercomputer centers - NYT.</title>
<headline>U.S. to back fewer supercomputer centers - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Science Foundation plans to reduce the number of supercomputer research centers it funds from four to two, the New York Times said on Monday.</p>
<p>Despite the decline, financing levels would not change much, the paper said, citing officials.</p>
<p>Total spending for each center would be about $170 million over five years, with $29 million budgeted for the first year, the paper said.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
